From 1734db0f16b29e049aace135e4d28b4cf40b627a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tominal <hello@kahusoftware.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:53:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat: expose the members a media key rollout did not reach

`EncryptionManager` already records which recipients a rollout reached,
keeps the rest in its `undelivered` map, and retries each one on backoff.
The list is public as far as `BaseRtcRoom::undelivered_key_members`, and
the upkeep consumes it internally, but no public type a host holds can
read it: `RtcCall` does not expose it and `LiveKitCall` keeps its
`RtcCall` private.

So a host can be in a call where nobody can decrypt anything it sends and
have no way to say so. It is the one fault in an encrypted call that the
person causing it cannot see for themselves, because their own audio and
video look fine locally.

Two delegating accessors, no new types and no new events:

- `RtcCall::undelivered_key_members`, beside
  `subscribe_own_membership_lapsed`, which reaches the same per-slot state
  by the same route.
- `LiveKitCall::undelivered_key_members`, delegating to it.

`matrix-rtc-core`'s own tests already pin the behaviour behind this,
`an_undelivered_key_is_retried_on_backoff_until_delivered` and
`an_undelivered_recipient_is_retried_without_making_signalling_unreachable`,
both reading the list through `BaseRtcRoom::undelivered_key_members`. What
is added here is reach rather than behaviour.

A push would be better than a poll: `EncryptionManager::subscribe_undelivered`
is already a `watch`, so a host could wake on a change rather than ask. It is
`pub(crate)` and its value type `Undelivered` is private, so exposing it is a
wider change than this one, and a caller that already wakes on membership
changes can ask then. Happy to send that version instead if you would rather
have it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/matrix-rtc-call-sdk/src/livekit/call.rs | 10 ++++++++++
 crates/matrix-rtc-call/src/client.rs           | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/matrix-rtc-call-sdk/src/livekit/call.rs b/crates/matrix-rtc-call-sdk/src/livekit/call.rs
index ac27e0b..a354618 100644
--- a/crates/matrix-rtc-call-sdk/src/livekit/call.rs
+++ b/crates/matrix-rtc-call-sdk/src/livekit/call.rs
@@ -570,6 +570,16 @@ impl LiveKitCall {
         self.bridge.key_for(identity).is_some()
     }
 
+    /// The members this call's media key has not reached yet, by member id
+    /// (034 R32); `None` once the call is no longer joined.
+    ///
+    /// Nobody in it can decrypt anything we send, so a host that wants to say
+    /// so needs the list. The core already keeps it and retries each one on
+    /// backoff; this only hands it out.
+    pub async fn undelivered_key_members(&self) -> Option<Vec<String>> {
+        self.call.undelivered_key_members().await
+    }
+
     /// Leave the call cleanly: send the leave event (cancelling the delayed
     /// leave) and close the SFU connection.
     ///
diff --git a/crates/matrix-rtc-call/src/client.rs b/crates/matrix-rtc-call/src/client.rs
index 963b839..51fdb07 100644
--- a/crates/matrix-rtc-call/src/client.rs
+++ b/crates/matrix-rtc-call/src/client.rs
@@ -1227,6 +1227,16 @@ impl<B: MatrixBackend + 'static> RtcCall<B> {
             .subscribe_own_membership_lapsed(&self.slot_id)
     }
 
+    /// The members a key rollout has not reached yet, by member id, retried
+    /// on backoff (034 R32); `None` once we are no longer joined.
+    pub async fn undelivered_key_members(&self) -> Option<Vec<String>> {
+        self.state
+            .lock()
+            .await
+            .rtc()
+            .undelivered_key_members(&self.slot_id)
+    }
+
     /// The slot's raised hands, oldest first.
     pub async fn raised_hands(&self) -> Vec<RaisedHand> {
         self.state
